athlib tendsto_integral_filter_of_dominated_convergence.) For s ∈ (0, ρ): y ↦ ζ_s(y)⟨ν(y), w⟩ is μ-a.e. strongly measurable (ζ_s is continuous and ν is μ-a.e. strongly measurable); |ζ_s(y)⟨ν(y), w⟩| ≤ 1_{B̄_ρ}(y) for μ-a.e. y (for y ∈ B_ρ use 0 ≤ ζ_s ≤ 1 and |⟨ν, w⟩| ≤ |ν||w| ≤ 1 μ-a.e.; for y ∉ B_ρ, ζ_s(y) = 0); and 1_{B̄_ρ} is μ-integrable by step 1. Pointwise: if y ∈ B_ρ, then for every s ∈ (|y − x|, ρ) we have y ∈ B_s, so ζ_s(y) = 1 and ζ_s(y)⟨ν(y), w⟩ = ⟨ν(y), w⟩ = 1_{B_ρ}(y)⟨ν(y), w⟩ eventually; if y ∉ B_ρ, then ζ_s(y)⟨ν(y), w⟩ = 0 = 1_{B_ρ}(y)⟨ν(y), w⟩ for all s ∈ (0, ρ). Hence ∫ ζ_s⟨ν, w⟩ dμ → ∫ 1_{B_ρ}⟨ν, w⟩ dμ = ∫_{B_ρ} ⟨ν, w⟩ dμ along 𝓝[<]ρ.\n\n6. Inequality (∗) holds for all s in the set (0, ρ), which belongs to 𝓝[<]ρ; by steps 4 and 5 and the preservation of non-strict inequalities under limits (Mathlib le_of_tendsto_of_tendsto), ∫_{B_ρ(x)} ⟨ν(y), w⟩ dμ(y) ≤ d. ∎",
